From 449cdc5e29c63aa66b41ce8c2783f6b0d84c62b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vítor Hugo Silva <vitorhg20080@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:29:28 +0000
Subject: hwmon: (ads7871) Add error handle from spi_setup()
Mime-version: 1.0
Content-type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-transfer-encoding: 8bit
Git-commit: 449cdc5e29c63aa66b41ce8c2783f6b0d84c62b0
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc4
References: git-fixes

The ads7871 probe() ignores the spi_setup() error return value
and it attempts to write to registers even if spi_setup() fails.

Return the setup error before accessing any registers.

AI was used for peer-review the patch.

Fixes: e0c70b8078629 ("hwmon: add TI ads7871 a/d converter driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Vítor Hugo Silva <vitorhg20080@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261118092928.163553-1-vitorhg20080@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck <linux@roeck-us.net>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/hwmon/ads7871.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/hwmon/ads7871.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/ads7871.c
@@ -168,7 +168,9 @@ static int ads7871_probe(struct spi_devi
 	/* Configure the SPI bus */
 	spi->mode = (SPI_MODE_0);
 	spi->bits_per_word = 8;
-	spi_setup(spi);
+	ret = spi_setup(spi);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	ads7871_write_reg8(spi, REG_SER_CONTROL, 0);
 	ads7871_write_reg8(spi, REG_AD_CONTROL, 0);
